1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,284
x402-avm: pay per call for MCP tools and APIs, on Algorand.

2
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:09,622
An agent calls a paid tool.

3
00:00:09,662 --> 00:00:14,057
The server answers HTTP 402 Payment Required, with a price.

4
00:00:14,447 --> 00:00:17,109
The client signs a two-transaction group:

5
00:00:17,149 --> 00:00:21,788
it pays exactly the price, and the server pays the 2,000 microALGO fee.

6
00:00:22,478 --> 00:00:25,912
The server verifies it by simulation and runs the tool.

7
00:00:25,952 --> 00:00:28,817
The payment settles only if the tool succeeds.

8
00:00:30,766 --> 00:00:33,788
With x402-algorand's ready-made signers,

9
00:00:33,828 --> 00:00:36,849
a FastAPI paywall is about thirty lines.

10
00:00:37,639 --> 00:00:44,596
For MCP, ai-economy-sdk's PaymentGate prices each tool, over Streamable HTTP.

11
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:52,914
A real run on LocalNet: a plain request gets a 402, for 10,000 microALGO.

12
00:00:53,904 --> 00:00:55,874
The HTTPX client pays it:

13
00:00:55,914 --> 00:00:59,411
the buyer's balance drops by exactly 10,000.

14
00:01:00,401 --> 00:01:06,484
The MCP quickstart: the tool answers, and the buyer pays exactly 5,000 microALGO.

15
00:01:07,674 --> 00:01:12,861
On the indexer: one atomic group, with the server's 2,000 microALGO fee.

16
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,695
Clients set spend controls, in Python and JavaScript.

17
00:01:18,735 --> 00:01:24,040
With a 10,000 cap, a 50,000 demand is refused before anything is signed.

18
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:28,238
TestNet and MainNet run the same code.

19
00:01:28,278 --> 00:01:33,194
Read-only examples simulate real ALGO and USDC payments, and spend nothing.

20
00:01:35,593 --> 00:01:39,659
The docs at x402-avm.github.io have full search:

21
00:01:39,699 --> 00:01:44,193
type “spend controls”, and land on the API reference.

22
00:01:45,109 --> 00:01:50,829
And llms.txt gives AI agents an index of every page, in Markdown.

23
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:54,700
Install the SDKs, and start on LocalNet.
